##Difference between int main() and int main(void) ?

  int main(void) - used when taking in strictly no terminal arguements - u will get to know
  int main() - used when taking terminal arguements

  terminal arguements are same as function arguements - 
  (analogy to arguements and parameters in python where the values are given at the time of EXECUTING the code)
  ./execute val1 val2

  whereas scanf are the input that are given at THE RUNTIME.


## Clearing input buffer in the whitepsace input : 
  for ONLY charecter input we add a white space while getting input
  Eg : scanf(" %c",input);  ---- scanf("_%c",input); the given underscore is the representation of whitespace
    

